Cases for a region kind that a dialect registers (ADR-2026-11-10-1941),
shared by the two validators' tests: `lean/FirTest/RegionKindCases.lean`
and `crates/funk-ir/tests/region_kind_cases.rs`. Each case starts with a
line of three equals signs, its verdict and its name. The verdict is
`accept`; `reject`, for a case that breaks a general rule; or
`reject-by-kind`, for a case where a region breaks the rule of its kind,
which both validators report as such. Each case parses and prints as
itself on both sides.

The cases run in the sum of the core and a test dialect named `toy`, with
two ops: `toy.graph`, which takes and gives nothing and owns one region of
the kind `toy.dataflow`, and `toy.node`, which takes any number of values
of one type `iN` and gives one of that type. The dialect registers the
kind `toy.dataflow`, whose ops are unordered. Its rule: the region holds
one block, which takes no arguments; every op of the block is an op of
`toy`, and no op of `toy` is a terminator, so no op ends the block; and
each value that an op of the block uses is a result of an op of the same
block, before or after it, or a parameter of the function.

=== accept a-node-uses-a-later-node
dialects toy

func @f(%p: i8) {
^entry:
  toy.graph { toy.dataflow
    ^g:
      %b: i8 = toy.node %a, %p @0
      %a: i8 = toy.node %p @0
  } @0
  ret @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
}
=== accept a-node-of-no-operands
dialects toy

func @f() {
^entry:
  toy.graph { toy.dataflow
    ^g:
      %a: i32 = toy.node @0
      %b: i32 = toy.node %a, %a, %a @0
  } @0
  ret @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
}
=== accept two-graphs-in-a-function
dialects toy

func @f(%p: i8) -> i8 {
^entry:
  %s: i8 = add %p, %p @0
  toy.graph { toy.dataflow
    ^g:
      %a: i8 = toy.node %p @0
  } @0
  toy.graph { toy.dataflow
    ^h:
      %b: i8 = toy.node %c @0
      %c: i8 = toy.node %p @0
  } @0
  ret %s @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
}
=== accept a-graph-inside-a-graph
dialects toy

func @f(%p: i8) {
^entry:
  toy.graph { toy.dataflow
    ^g:
      toy.graph { toy.dataflow
        ^h:
          %b: i8 = toy.node %p @0
      } @0
      %a: i8 = toy.node %p @0
  } @0
  ret @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
}
